1. She has difficulty visualizing faces, including her own, and likely has prosopagnosia (face blindness). (Verbatim: "I can't see faces... I can't picture it. Um, just quite sad, but I try and take photos. I can't picture my own face.")

2. She cannot mentally picture images of people’s faces, even of close family like her parents. (Verbatim: "if I was to try and picture my parents' faces or anyone I know's faces, I- I can't- I can't picture it.")

3. She relies heavily on photographs to remember people and experiences due to her face blindness. (Verbatim: "so that's why I think photos are great... I took a lot so that I could, like, um, print out a bunch.")

4. She owns a Polaroid printer to print out photos. (Verbatim: "I have a, um, what you call it, um, Polaroid printer.")

5. She can remember and visualize dogs’ faces and appearances better than human faces. (Verbatim: "i said like you know how i can't picture people i can picture dogs so i know her dog friends")

6. She previously considered getting a Shiba Inu instead of her current dog. (Verbatim: "i was close to getting a shiba instead of a samoyed")

7. She owns a Samoyed dog. (Verbatim: "if i didn't have a samoyed i'd i'd have a shiba")

8. She has a strong preference for taking and collecting photos, especially during travels. (Verbatim: "I took... thousands, I ran out of space on my drive, and then I had to upgrade it.")

9. She finds Japan very clean and reflective, which made photographing difficult. (Verbatim: "Turns out Japan is very reflective. Everything's so clean and shiny.")

10. She struggles more with hot, humid weather and experienced extreme heat during a visit to Japan. (Verbatim: "I was melting the whole time. I was super melting. Um, yeah, it was a heat wave.") [end of text]



